# EMPTY STATES

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

Every empty state should guide the athlete.

An empty screen is not an error.

It is an opportunity to explain what happens next.

The athlete should never wonder:

"What am I supposed to do now?"

---

# Core Principle

Explain.

Guide.

Reassure.

Never leave the athlete without direction.

---

# Philosophy

Empty states are part of the coaching experience.

CAS should behave like an experienced coach.

If information is unavailable,

the athlete receives:

- an explanation;
- the reason when known;
- the next recommended action.

---

# Primary Rule

Every empty state answers three questions:

What happened?

Why?

What should I do next?

---

# Tone

Calm.

Professional.

Respectful.

Never humorous.

Never sarcastic.

Never alarming.

---

# Visual Hierarchy

Every empty state contains:

Illustration or icon (optional)

↓

Short title

↓

One concise explanation

↓

One primary action

↓

Optional secondary action

Nothing more.

